You know what's fun is some
of those stories are fun

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:56.993
'cause you forget some of the stuff.

00:08:56.993 --> 00:08:59.730
So that was Sean Courtney
story I completely remember now

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:02.623
that it was like, that's 1984 shit.

00:09:04.036 --> 00:09:06.503
I always believed in
kindness even back then.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:08.920
Anyway, let's keep it going.

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:11.470
Hi, Sarah.

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:12.880
- Hey, Gary.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.320
- How are things?

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.030
- Things are really
good on the west coast.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:18.940
- It's early.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:20.750
Thanks for getting up early.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.053
- Yeah, whatever it takes, of course.

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:27.637
So four years in the
making since I tweeted you,

00:09:27.637 --> 00:09:29.130
and you tweeted back.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.440
- So for everybody who's
watching right now,

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:32.900
yesterday, I think you tweeted right?

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.760
- Yeah, I just responded to the tweet,

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.210
which was like four years ago,

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:37.097
Sarah said something I said,

00:09:37.097 --> 00:09:38.200
"Well, we should talk then."

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:41.390
And yesterday, she retweeted
it and wrote over it,

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:42.380
it's like, "Can we book this?"

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:44.460
And I saw it, I'm like,
"Yep, let's book it."

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:45.550
And here we are.

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:46.800
- What's so funny, Gary

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:49.367
is then your team messaged me and says,

00:09:49.367 --> 00:09:50.840
"Just get ready with a question."

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:53.560
And I thought this is
what's so funny is that,

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.510
I have obviously known about
that tweet for four years

00:09:56.510 --> 00:10:00.680
and every time I thought about
messaging you in the past.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:03.710
It was because I wanted something.

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:06.057
And then I would do this
thing where I'm like,

00:10:06.057 --> 00:10:07.270
"What's he gonna tell me?"

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:08.103
He's gonna tell me, "Start
the YouTube channel."

00:10:08.103 --> 00:10:10.409
He's gonna tell me (mumbles)

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:11.740
So just do the thing.

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:12.950
And then yesterday,

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:15.730
we were supposed to have
our 10 year celebration

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:17.177
at the organization I'm with.

00:10:17.177 --> 00:10:20.870
And I was sitting in my house
not feeling sorry for myself,

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:21.703
but just thinking,

00:10:21.703 --> 00:10:24.150
"Damn, I was supposed
to be at that party."

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:24.983
And I'm here

00:10:24.983 --> 00:10:28.113
and look what we've done during
the pandemic for our kids.

00:10:29.092 --> 00:10:32.747
And I was like, "We haven't
been a victim during this time.

00:10:32.747 --> 00:10:33.947
"We've been so resourceful.

00:10:33.947 --> 00:10:37.277
"We've been just doing such a great job

00:10:37.277 --> 00:10:38.460
"and just on it."

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:40.530
And I thought, "I just
gotta tell him, thank you."

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:41.740
So that's why I did it.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:44.166
So then when they messaged me, they're

00:10:44.166 --> 00:10:45.416
"Do you have a question?"

00:10:46.408 --> 00:10:47.600
I mean, I have thought of them obviously,

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.433
I've had time to think of it.

00:10:48.433 --> 00:10:49.266
But I was like,

00:10:49.266 --> 00:10:50.810
"Wait, that's not even
why I did it this time."

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:52.860
- You know what's so powerful about that,

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:54.310
the other times you've thought about it,

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:56.200
it was from a place of need.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.530
- Yes.

00:10:57.530 --> 00:10:59.630
- Yesterday was from a place of giving

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:01.640
and the universe decided

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.800
to serendipitously allow me to see it.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:07.430
And then it creates the moment

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.170
and I really mean this,

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:10.763
that shit fucking freaks me out.

00:11:10.763 --> 00:11:12.970
When I hear that story,

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:14.540
it really makes me believe

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:17.710
there's just something so obvious.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.880
No different, I'm sure you're
just watching with Abel.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:23.540
Abel still feels the impact
of a third grade fight

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:26.686
that I stopped out of kindness.

00:11:26.686 --> 00:11:28.990
Good brings on more good

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:30.420
and bad brings on more bad

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:31.410
and I believe in that shit

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.720
and I feel a huge sense of responsibility

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:35.230
as a good communicator

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:38.060
that people are associated with

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:40.360
and attracted to and drawn to,

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:41.870
to put out as much good as possible.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:44.070
When I hear that story from you just now.

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:46.960
It fucking reinforces what I believe.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:49.300
- I mean, it's eight minutes later

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.257
and then the funny thing was
the tweets rolling in like

00:11:51.257 --> 00:11:52.707
"Oh, she's been holding that, like she's."

00:11:52.707 --> 00:11:54.880
I'm like, "It's not like that."

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:57.700
- It happens all the time.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.030
I feel horrible 'cause sometimes I see it

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.190
but I'm not in that mindset.

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:03.620
Attempt number 494

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:07.220
to get Gary Vee to follow
me or say hi, it's hard.

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:09.030
I'm out here operating and navigating

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:10.253
and trying my best and,

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:14.630
5000 texts a day, 10,000 DMS a day,

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.083
thousands of tweets.

00:12:17.085 --> 00:12:20.263
You'll never beat the math
but my intent is there and,

00:12:21.457 --> 00:12:24.800
you make lemonade out of these lemons.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:27.370
This whole pandemic has let me connect

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:28.817
with the community at a level,

00:12:28.817 --> 00:12:31.383
"Tea With GaryVee" is
a connection point that

00:12:31.383 --> 00:12:35.150
is greater than "#AskGaryVee"

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:36.400
is greater than anything I've done,

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:37.780
I think, really, honestly.

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:41.740
It's got a different level of
depth and calmness and speed

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:42.860
that I think is really connected

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:45.410
and helped both me and
everybody who's watching it.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:50.870
- I'm grateful and I was
thinking last night about how,

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.590
I started this non-profit in 2008.

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:56.873
I had been laid off and
when this whole thing hits,

00:12:58.211 --> 00:12:59.763
75 days ago.

00:13:01.679 --> 00:13:03.190
I remember when I was in New York

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:04.690
and I flew back to California.

00:13:07.356 --> 00:13:09.743
You were talking about this
in one of your shows recently.

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.413
I didn't get nervous.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:16.140
- You were there.
- I built this in 2008.

00:13:17.643 --> 00:13:20.740
No noise and my brother, an entrepreneur

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:22.180
in his own right in real estate.

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:24.360
He introduced me to you 10 years ago,

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.453
and sometimes we'll be hanging out,

00:13:25.453 --> 00:13:27.000
I'll be like,

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.627
He's like, "Don't be a victim,

00:13:28.627 --> 00:13:29.460
"don't be a victim."

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:30.711
I'm like, "Fair."

00:13:30.711 --> 00:13:33.294
(Sarah laughs)

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:36.330
- The big thing for everybody
who likes to complain

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:37.930
and dwell and be a victim.

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:41.560
They need to realize that nobody cares

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.830
'cause they're worried
about their own problems.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.910
And the only people that
are caring and coddling you

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:51.263
are the people that extremely
love you and enable it.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:55.100
Or other people that are fucking losing.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.060
Complaining and dwelling is a bad formula,

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:00.550
because it creates too bad relationships.

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:02.870
It creates a relationship
with another losing player

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:04.190
and you're just negative on negative

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:08.150
and you're just hanging out
in your fucking sorrow bubble.

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:11.350
Or it's putting somebody
that loves you so much

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:13.950
in a precarious spot where
they're enabling you,

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:17.023
which eventually leads to
resentment by both parties.

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:20.380
Complaining and dwelling is bad.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.750
It really hurts relationships.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.940
- And people that love you
don't want you to sit in that.

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:26.773
And it's interesting

00:14:26.773 --> 00:14:28.345
'cause I don't know if you know what I do.

00:14:28.345 --> 00:14:30.510
But I mean, I help teens
become entrepreneurs.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:32.490
We start them teens, tweening,

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:35.390
and you'll be happy to know that,

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:38.300
our teams run our social media,

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:40.720
because there is no
excuse for not having it

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:44.240
but I personally do not
feel Tik Tok is my jam--

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:46.480
- It is so your jam.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:48.330
- I'm saying the kids--

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:49.593
- They totally know it.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:52.600
But in four hours, it could be your jam.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:53.810
- Yes and they'll teach me.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:55.610
The fun thing is to be in situations

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:58.777
where I can go to our to our
kids, our teens, our tweens--

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:01.730
- Sarah, let me take this moment

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:02.800
because I'm gonna help a lot of people.

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:04.310
Lemme tell you how to get taught

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:06.470
on Tik Tok, Snapchat, LinkedIn

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:09.070
or the next three things that
happen in the next decade.

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:11.840
You go immediately and you consume content

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:13.910
on the platform for 10 hours.

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:15.930
And then you make 10 pieces of content.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.270
10 hours, 10 pieces of content,

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.120
is how you learn every platform.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:22.630
Go in, download it, read it.

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:23.463
Don't judge them.

00:15:23.463 --> 00:15:24.400
Don't say it's stupid.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:28.600
10 hours of consuming
10 pieces of content,

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.130
giving it your best,

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:31.330
and then reassess.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:33.310
10 hours 10 piece of content

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:36.720
is how every single person can
learn a new social network.

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:38.250
- Well, you should check it out,

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:40.490
because they were shouting
you out yesterday.

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:41.323
- I will check it out.

00:15:41.323 --> 00:15:42.430
(Sarah laughs)

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:43.350
- It is such a pleasure.

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:44.730
I'm glad we did this.

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:47.010
- Yeah, thanks and everybody.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:47.860
I wanna thank you, Gary,

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:49.740
you gave a tip in a video recently

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:53.420
about just reaching out to
people in the DMS on Instagram,

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:56.250
and we're doing a virtual
entrepreneurship summer camp.

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:58.830
And I've reached out to
celebrity entrepreneurs

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:03.200
in every space and we've
had some great yeses.

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:04.710
That would probably not be chillin'

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:06.010
at their house right now.

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:07.960
- Can't get a yes if you don't ask.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:09.490
- Yeah, so thank you, Gary.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:10.323
- Take care.

00:16:10.323 --> 00:16:11.156
Bye bye.

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.350
Dustin, what are the updated numbers?

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:15.730
I wanna start creating the competition.

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:18.840
I wanna get Twitter,
YouTube, Facebook and Twitch,

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:21.350
to start sharing their
URLs to their community

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.480
to get to the highest number.

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:24.440
We might have to do a pizza
party for the best guest.

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:25.290
- Pizza party, cool.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:26.250
- So where are we at?

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.370
- YouTube is 3000.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:32.500
Facebook is 2800, it's close.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:35.300
Twitch looks like it's 330.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:39.430
And Twitter looks about 330 or 20ish also.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:41.110
- Twitter and Twitch have some work to do.

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:42.410
Okay, let's keep it going.

00:16:45.578 --> 00:16:47.160
Katie?

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:48.660
- Hello, how are you?

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:52.090
- I'm very well, but your
beautiful setting is inspiring.

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:53.500
- It's the best place to be.

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:54.340
- Good for you.

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:56.150
It's really nice to see you.

00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:58.100
- You too, I'm so excited.

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:01.210
I've been playing, what
would Gary say all week.

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:02.550
So all of my questions,

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:04.310
I filtered through what
your response would be.

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:06.860
And I've made a bunch
of changes this week.

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:08.563
But my question is--

00:17:08.563 --> 00:17:10.374
- And did you feel any impact
of any of those changes yet?

00:17:10.374 --> 00:17:11.520
I mean, it's early.

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:12.353
You have?

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.200
Gimme one example.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.400
- So we have a farm market,

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:18.980
and we do home delivery
throughout the capital region,

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:19.983
upstate New York.

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:26.050
And obviously, all food
delivery has skyrocketed

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.100
in the last few weeks.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:32.940
And, we're just growing
so exponentially that

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:35.860
it was scattered,

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:37.380
so we were--

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:38.970
- Of course, when chaos hits,

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:42.200
I mean, it's happening at
WineText right now, Katie.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:44.360
We hired nine.

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:47.240
The Springfield New Jersey
pool shut down for the summer.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:50.145
So we hired all nine lifeguards,

00:17:50.145 --> 00:17:52.260
and inevitably, some of those kids

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:54.260
are gonna ship the wrong bottle of wine.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.160
When it gets to chaos,

00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:00.700
the big key Katie, is
to not beat yourself up.

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:02.780
If somebody gets corn instead of apples,

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:04.360
you could always fix anything

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:06.453
by saying you're sorry and addressing it.

00:18:07.367 --> 00:18:09.590
And I think too many people
worry about perfection

00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:11.360
or if we deliver the wrong thing,

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.430
it gets put on Facebook
and everybody gets mad.

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:16.430
I'm sorry and meaning it

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.420
is the greatest antidote

00:18:18.420 --> 00:18:21.900
to anxiety around making a
mistake in business and in life.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:24.640
- Yeah and I try to be super transparent.

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:26.053
We went from just me,

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:30.130
I had knee surgery on February 11th.

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:32.320
And then, three days later,

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:34.430
I was delivering things I
couldn't even put a shoe on yet.

00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:35.333
So that was cool.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:37.810
I was all right, people need food.

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:38.990
So we're gonna get food out.

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:40.173
- I'm impressed.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:47.740
- I'm like 30x what I
was January, February.

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:48.633
- Have you hired?

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.243
- Yes, that's my challenge.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:56.230
People don't like to show
up to work sometimes.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.450
- A lot of times.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:19:00.763
We hired four people last
week, and only one showed up.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:05.060
And Brandon, my best
friend who has great EQ,

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:08.250
hired as well and really
communicated well.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:11.430
I think what it comes down
to is not dwelling on that,

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:14.070
recognizing that's going
to be part of the game,

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:17.970
learning and hiring a couple
more people than you need,

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:19.940
just in case they don't
show up in the first day

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:21.450
or quit after day one.

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:24.183
Both happen, no show
and quit after day one.

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:27.452
But the reality is you just keep pushing.

00:19:27.452 --> 00:19:30.540
I think Facebook, Craigslist, LinkedIn

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:33.190
are all good places to get individuals.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:35.486
I think emailing all your customers

00:19:35.486 --> 00:19:37.050
and saying, "We're hiring."

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.070
Some of those people wanna get

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.780
their teenage kids out of the house.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:42.500
So I think there's some hacks there.

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:45.800
- Yeah and I've done a little
bit of outsourcing too,

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:47.890
so that I don't have to
do everything in house.

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:49.000
- Good job.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:53.140
- And I simplified things
because I was like,

00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:56.530
it ends up I'm pretty much
the primary delivery person.

00:19:56.530 --> 00:19:58.570
And we're doing a big range

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:01.490
